# Normalise line endings to LF everywhere, in the repo *and* in the working
# tree on every platform. Without this, a Windows checkout with the common
# `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites every LF to CRLF on disk, which silently
# corrupts the golden test fixtures: their exact bytes are the thing under
# test, so `tests/adapters/test_httpx.py::test_blank_lines_are_ignored_not_skipped`
# (which asserts a real blank line exists in the raw JSON-lines fixture)
# fails on Windows and passes on Linux, for no reason visible in the code.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixtures are captured tool output — byte-exact by definition. Never let
# any heuristic touch them.
tests/fixtures/** -text
